==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*per-|id=fare|*(s)twerH-}}
From Late {{inh|en|enm|perturben|t=to disturb (someone) mentally, disquiet; to cause disorder to (something), confuse; to hinder (something)}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=perturben|pos=v|id=MED33142}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|perturber}}, and from its {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|la|perturbāre}}, the {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|active}} {{glossary|infinitive}} of {{m|la|perturbō|t=to confuse; to alarm, disturb, trouble, perturb}}, from {{m|la|per-|pos={{glossary|intensifying}} {{glossary|prefix}}}} + {{m|la|turbō|t=to agitate, disturb, unsettle, perturb; to upset}}<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=5304084336|date=March 2025|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref> (from {{m|la|turba|t=disorder, disturbance, turmoil}} (possibly from {{der|en|grc|τῠ́ρβη|t=confusion, disorder, tumult}}, either from {{der|en|qsb-grc}}, or {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)twerH-|t=to agitate, stir up; to urge on, propel}}) + {{m|la|-ō|pos=suffix forming {{glossary|infinitive}}s of regular first-{{glossary|conjugation}} {{glossary|verb}}s}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pəˈtɜːb/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/pəɹˈtɜɹb/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-perturb.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)b|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|per|turb}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[disturb]]; to bother or unsettle.
#: {{syn|en|agitate|unsettle|Thesaurus:upset}}
# {{lb|en|physics}} To slightly modify the motion of an object.
# {{lb|en|astronomy}} To modify the motion of a body by exerting a gravitational force.
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} To modify slightly, such as an equation or value.

